WEBVTT

00:00:01.919 --> 00:00:05.286
Captain's Log, Stardate 47410.2.

00:00:05.322 --> 00:00:07.722
The Atrean government
has requested assistance

00:00:07.758 --> 00:00:09.453
in averting a natural disaster.

00:00:09.493 --> 00:00:11.688
Two of their geologists
have come aboard

00:00:11.728 --> 00:00:15.824
one of whom is a human who
has been living on Atrea IV.

00:00:15.866 --> 00:00:17.561
Captain, the situation
has worsened

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:19.899
since my husband and I
first contacted you.

00:00:20.003 --> 00:00:23.905
The molten core of our planet
isn't just cooling...

00:00:23.941 --> 00:00:25.772
it's begun to solidify.

00:00:25.809 --> 00:00:28.243
Our gravitational field
has been affected.

00:00:28.278 --> 00:00:31.441
Seismic activity has increased
by a factor of three.

00:00:31.481 --> 00:00:34.473
If the cooling
continues at this rate

00:00:34.518 --> 00:00:38.181
Atrea will become uninhabitable
in 13 months.

00:00:38.221 --> 00:00:39.916
We could minimize

00:00:39.957 --> 00:00:43.620
seismic activity by creating
isobaric fissures and relieving

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:44.820
some of the tectonic stress

00:00:44.861 --> 00:00:46.624
but that would just
be a temporary fix.

00:00:46.663 --> 00:00:50.121
The only permanent solution
would be to reliquefy the core.

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:52.260
These pockets
in the magma layer...

00:00:52.302 --> 00:00:53.428
how close are they

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.529
to the molten region
of the core?

00:00:55.572 --> 00:00:57.563
A few kilometers. Why?

00:00:57.607 --> 00:00:59.302
Data, you think
that's close enough

00:00:59.343 --> 00:01:00.674
for ferroplasmic infusion?

00:01:02.279 --> 00:01:04.679
The procedure will involve
using the ship's phasers

00:01:04.715 --> 00:01:06.683
to drill down
through the planet's surface

00:01:06.717 --> 00:01:08.548
into the pockets,
where we would set up

00:01:08.585 --> 00:01:10.883
a series of plasma
infusion units.

00:01:10.921 --> 00:01:12.320
We'll trigger the units

00:01:12.356 --> 00:01:14.347
by firing modulated
energy bursts

00:01:14.391 --> 00:01:15.881
down through the shafts.

00:01:15.926 --> 00:01:17.052
I see.

00:01:17.094 --> 00:01:20.393
Injecting plasma
directly into the core

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:23.058
should trigger a chain reaction

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.898
and that will reliquefy
the magma.

00:01:26.003 --> 00:01:27.368
It should be possible

00:01:27.404 --> 00:01:29.531
to stabilize
the core temperature

00:01:29.573 --> 00:01:30.835
at 93% of normal.

00:01:30.874 --> 00:01:31.863
If it works

00:01:31.908 --> 00:01:34.035
the core would remain
molten for centuries.

00:01:34.077 --> 00:01:38.377
If you'll give your permission,
we could begin immediately.

00:01:38.415 --> 00:01:39.473
Very well.

00:01:39.516 --> 00:01:40.915
But before we proceed

00:01:40.951 --> 00:01:43.818
I'd like to update
our geological surveys.

00:01:43.854 --> 00:01:46.687
Fine. I'd be very happy to help
you with that, Doctor.

00:01:46.723 --> 00:01:48.918
We've assigned you quarters
during our time here.

00:01:48.959 --> 00:01:50.517
Please make yourselves
comfortable.

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:52.255
Thank you, Captain.

00:01:54.031 --> 00:01:55.430
Data?

00:01:55.465 --> 00:01:56.955
Yes, Doctor.

00:01:58.402 --> 00:02:01.166
Do you have any idea who I am?

00:02:01.204 --> 00:02:03.195
You are Dr. Juliana Tainer.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:07.768
Oh, you lost
all your early memories.

00:02:07.811 --> 00:02:10.336
We thought you would,
but we couldn't be certain.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.405
Have we met before?

00:02:12.449 --> 00:02:14.383
Oh, Data, I was there

00:02:14.418 --> 00:02:17.876
right at the beginning
on Omicron Theta.

00:02:17.988 --> 00:02:20.320
I helped create you.

00:02:20.357 --> 00:02:24.157
And now... look at you.

00:02:24.194 --> 00:02:26.355
You were a colleague
of Dr. Soong?

00:02:26.396 --> 00:02:29.888
I most certainly was...

00:02:29.933 --> 00:02:32.766
and I was also his wife.

00:02:32.803 --> 00:02:35.738
In a way, I suppose
you could say

00:02:35.772 --> 00:02:38.707
I am your mother.

00:03:09.839 --> 00:03:14.242
Space, the final frontier.

00:03:14.276 --> 00:03:18.110
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:03:18.147 --> 00:03:20.115
Its continuing mission...

00:03:20.149 --> 00:03:24.085
to explore strange new worlds

00:03:24.119 --> 00:03:28.556
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:03:28.591 --> 00:03:32.925
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:04:31.386 --> 00:04:34.753
I just can't believe
I'm seeing you like this again

00:04:34.789 --> 00:04:37.485
after all these years.

00:04:37.525 --> 00:04:39.356
Doctor, I have no memory of you.

00:04:39.394 --> 00:04:41.294
Oh, there's a reason for that.

00:04:41.329 --> 00:04:42.887
We wiped your processors

00:04:42.964 --> 00:04:45.831
after we finished
refining your programming.

00:04:45.867 --> 00:04:48.563
Why don't you tell me
what you do remember

00:04:48.603 --> 00:04:50.594
and then I'll fill in the gaps.

00:04:50.638 --> 00:04:52.105
My memory record begins

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:54.700
when I was activated
by the Starfleet officers

00:04:54.742 --> 00:04:56.835
on the Omicron Theta outpost.

00:04:56.878 --> 00:05:00.143
Ah, after the attack
of the Crystalline Entity.

00:05:00.181 --> 00:05:03.082
Yes. All of the inhabitants
of the colony were killed.

00:05:03.117 --> 00:05:05.142
However, I discovered
that my memory banks

00:05:05.186 --> 00:05:07.620
contain the contents
of their journals and logs.

00:05:07.655 --> 00:05:10.852
We hoped their experiences
would be useful.

00:05:10.925 --> 00:05:12.324
After your childhood

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:15.796
we figured you could use
all the help you could get.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:16.854
"My childhood?"

00:05:16.965 --> 00:05:19.490
Oh, well,
that's what I called it.

00:05:19.534 --> 00:05:22.503
Well, you were
like a baby, at first...

00:05:22.537 --> 00:05:26.871
a 100-kilogram baby, but still.

00:05:26.941 --> 00:05:32.709
You had trouble, uh, learning
your motor skills

00:05:32.747 --> 00:05:36.046
learning how to process
sensory information

00:05:36.084 --> 00:05:39.383
and, of course, Noonien
was never satisfied.

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:40.614
He kept tinkering

00:05:40.655 --> 00:05:43.783
trying you to make you
as human as possible.

00:05:43.825 --> 00:05:46.885
So you wiped
my memory processors

00:05:46.961 --> 00:05:49.191
after this "childhood"?

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:50.527
Mm-hmm.

00:05:50.565 --> 00:05:52.533
Then we deactivated you

00:05:52.567 --> 00:05:56.367
and programmed you
with the colonists' logs.

00:05:56.404 --> 00:05:58.497
We had planned to reactivate you

00:05:58.539 --> 00:06:00.370
but we never got the chance.

00:06:00.408 --> 00:06:03.206
That's when
the Crystalline Entity attacked.

00:06:03.244 --> 00:06:05.041
We had to leave quickly.

00:06:05.079 --> 00:06:07.274
We wanted to take you with us

00:06:07.315 --> 00:06:11.046
but there was only room for two
in the escape pod.

00:06:11.085 --> 00:06:15.784
Doctor, I have scanned
the journals of the colonists.

00:06:15.823 --> 00:06:19.816
There is only one Juliana
mentioned in them.

00:06:19.861 --> 00:06:22.455
Her last name was O'Donnell.

00:06:22.497 --> 00:06:24.465
That's me.

00:06:24.499 --> 00:06:28.299
But there was no mention that
my father was married to you.

00:06:28.336 --> 00:06:30.668
Because of my mother.

00:06:30.705 --> 00:06:32.639
She thought

00:06:32.673 --> 00:06:35.141
that Noonien was
an eccentric scientist

00:06:35.176 --> 00:06:36.871
who was far too old for me.

00:06:36.978 --> 00:06:38.843
We decided to marry secretly

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:42.509
to give her a chance to get
used to our being together.

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:46.179
We slipped away to Mavala IV
and got married there.

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:50.554
A Klingon and a Corvallan trader
were our witnesses.

00:06:50.591 --> 00:06:54.789
It wasn't exactly the wedding
I'd hoped for, but...

00:06:56.097 --> 00:06:57.792
Somehow, Noonien had a way

00:06:57.832 --> 00:07:00.892
of making even the oddest things
seem romantic.

00:07:00.935 --> 00:07:04.803
My father did have an unusual
way of looking at things.

00:07:04.839 --> 00:07:06.704
How would you know that?

00:07:06.741 --> 00:07:09.505
I encountered him once
in the Terlina system.

00:07:09.544 --> 00:07:12.843
Why, that's where we went to,
after we left the outpost.

00:07:12.914 --> 00:07:15.109
I'd no idea
that you'd even met him.

00:07:15.149 --> 00:07:17.913
It was shortly before his death.

00:07:21.155 --> 00:07:23.020
He's dead?

00:07:23.057 --> 00:07:25.389
Yes.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:32.861
I had no idea
it would hit me this hard.

00:07:32.934 --> 00:07:36.461
We didn't exactly part
on the best of terms.

00:07:36.504 --> 00:07:38.563
What do you mean?

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:44.237
Oh, I realized he loved his work

00:07:44.278 --> 00:07:46.143
as much as he loved me...

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:48.808
maybe more.

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:51.318
Oh, there we were
stuck out on this planet

00:07:51.352 --> 00:07:53.013
in the middle of the jungle

00:07:53.054 --> 00:07:55.648
with no one else to talk to...

00:07:55.690 --> 00:08:00.491
no... life.

00:08:04.532 --> 00:08:07.729
It just wasn't enough.

00:08:07.768 --> 00:08:10.566
That's why I left.

00:08:10.605 --> 00:08:15.804
But that was all
a very, very long time ago.

00:08:15.843 --> 00:08:20.644
The important thing is
that we're here now, together

00:08:20.681 --> 00:08:22.842
and I do want to get
to know you.

00:08:22.917 --> 00:08:26.683
This has been
an interesting encounter

00:08:26.721 --> 00:08:29.281
and an altogether
unexpected one.

00:08:29.323 --> 00:08:31.814
I would like

00:08:31.859 --> 00:08:35.226
to corroborate your story
before we proceed further.

00:08:35.263 --> 00:08:37.026
Excuse me, Doctor.

00:08:46.908 --> 00:08:50.400
Data, I'm almost finished
reconfiguring the phaser banks.

00:08:50.444 --> 00:08:52.878
We should be able to start
drilling in about an hour.

00:08:52.947 --> 00:08:54.744
Inform me when you are ready.

00:08:54.782 --> 00:08:57.012
What is it
you're doing over there?

00:08:57.051 --> 00:08:58.780
I am attempting to ascertain

00:08:58.819 --> 00:09:01.049
whether Dr. Tainer's
story is true.

00:09:01.088 --> 00:09:03.147
Don't you believe her?

00:09:03.191 --> 00:09:05.182
I neither believe nor doubt.

00:09:05.226 --> 00:09:08.024
I am simply trying
to verify her assertions.

00:09:09.864 --> 00:09:11.729
Well, what have you
turned up so far?

00:09:11.766 --> 00:09:13.563
The registrar's office
on Mavala IV

00:09:13.601 --> 00:09:16.297
cannot confirm whether
Dr. Soong was married there.

00:09:16.337 --> 00:09:18.498
Apparently, many
of the documents were lost

00:09:18.539 --> 00:09:20.336
when the government
was overthrown.

00:09:20.374 --> 00:09:21.773
What's that you're looking at?

00:09:21.809 --> 00:09:24.004
I am checking
passenger manifests

00:09:24.045 --> 00:09:27.276
to see if they went to Mavala IV
during the period in question.

00:09:29.283 --> 00:09:32.480
"O'Donnell, Juliana."

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:35.614
"Soong, Noonien."

00:09:35.656 --> 00:09:39.251
They were both passengers
on a transport which traveled

00:09:39.293 --> 00:09:43.127
from Omicron Theta to Mavala
and returned four days later.

00:09:43.164 --> 00:09:46.133
That sure fits with her story.

00:09:46.167 --> 00:09:48.965
Still, the fact
that they went to Mavala

00:09:49.003 --> 00:09:51.164
does not prove
they were married there.

00:09:53.641 --> 00:09:55.609
You know, Data,
it almost seems to me

00:09:55.643 --> 00:09:57.110
like you're trying to prove

00:09:57.144 --> 00:09:59.374
that Dr. Tainer
wasn't telling the truth.

00:09:59.413 --> 00:10:01.005
Not at all.

00:10:01.048 --> 00:10:03.141
I am merely unable
to reconcile her story

00:10:03.184 --> 00:10:06.051
with the fact that my father
never mentioned her to me.

00:10:06.087 --> 00:10:07.679
Well, she did leave him.

00:10:07.722 --> 00:10:10.520
Maybe she broke his heart.

00:10:10.558 --> 00:10:13.550
Maybe he just didn't
want to talk about her.

00:10:13.594 --> 00:10:14.993
Let me ask you this.

00:10:15.029 --> 00:10:18.556
Dr. Soong created
an emotion chip for you

00:10:18.599 --> 00:10:19.759
and didn't Lore tell you

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:21.734
that that chip also
contained memories...

00:10:21.769 --> 00:10:23.760
memories Soong
wanted you to have?

00:10:23.804 --> 00:10:25.169
Yes.

00:10:25.206 --> 00:10:29.506
It is possible that those
are memories of my childhood

00:10:29.543 --> 00:10:30.908
and of Mrs. Soong.

00:10:30.978 --> 00:10:33.879
And when you think about it,
why would she want to lie?

00:10:33.914 --> 00:10:36.747
Why would anybody want
to pretend to be your mother?

00:10:38.019 --> 00:10:40.510
I can think of no motive
for such a pretense.

00:10:40.554 --> 00:10:42.351
You know, I can understand

00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:46.554
that this might all be a little
disconcerting for you, Data.

00:10:46.594 --> 00:10:48.186
It came out of the blue

00:10:48.229 --> 00:10:51.460
and it doesn't fit
into your logical processors.

00:10:51.499 --> 00:10:52.693
That is true.

00:10:52.733 --> 00:10:54.223
But that's life, Data.

00:10:54.268 --> 00:10:57.863
Part of being human is learning
how to deal with the unexpected.

00:10:57.905 --> 00:11:00.032
To risk new experiences

00:11:00.074 --> 00:11:04.511
even when they don't fit
into your preconceptions.

00:11:04.545 --> 00:11:06.979
I admit
I am finding it difficult

00:11:07.014 --> 00:11:09.608
to accept the possibility
of a past

00:11:09.650 --> 00:11:11.709
about which I know nothing.

00:11:11.752 --> 00:11:16.917
But it is also true I am curious
to learn more about it.

00:11:33.107 --> 00:11:34.369
Data?

00:11:34.408 --> 00:11:39.675
I would like
to get to know you better...

00:11:39.714 --> 00:11:41.511
Mother.

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:51.022
I wanted to make you female

00:11:51.059 --> 00:11:53.425
but your father insisted
on a son.

00:11:53.461 --> 00:11:56.055
Oh, we argued about it endlessly

00:11:56.097 --> 00:11:58.691
right up until we were
ready to assemble you.

00:11:58.733 --> 00:12:00.030
How did you decide?

00:12:00.068 --> 00:12:02.832
Oh, Noonien walked in
with your head in his hand

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:05.862
and, innocent as you please,
said it was up to me.

00:12:05.907 --> 00:12:08.705
Well, he knew perfectly well
what he was doing.

00:12:08.743 --> 00:12:11.473
Once again, he had made it
in his own image.

00:12:11.512 --> 00:12:13.412
I mean, what could I
possibly say?

00:12:14.816 --> 00:12:16.181
Deanna Troi?

00:12:16.217 --> 00:12:18.447
Is that who you're going
to visit?

00:12:18.486 --> 00:12:19.885
Yes.

00:12:19.921 --> 00:12:22.389
Oh, your father
would be so pleased.

00:12:22.423 --> 00:12:23.720
Pleased?

00:12:23.758 --> 00:12:25.487
Well, he was worried

00:12:25.526 --> 00:12:26.891
that the sexuality program

00:12:26.995 --> 00:12:28.929
he designed for you
wouldn't work.

00:12:30.398 --> 00:12:31.865
You misunderstand.

00:12:31.899 --> 00:12:33.890
Counselor Troi is a therapist.

00:12:33.968 --> 00:12:35.629
Good night.

00:12:45.913 --> 00:12:48.780
We will be in position
over the drilling site

00:12:48.816 --> 00:12:50.716
in three minutes, 29 seconds.

00:12:50.752 --> 00:12:53.186
These scans indicate
that the magma pockets

00:12:53.221 --> 00:12:56.122
where we planned to set up
the infusion units

00:12:56.157 --> 00:12:57.749
are somewhat unstable.

00:12:57.792 --> 00:13:00.420
Well, I'm going to monitor
the density of the rock layers

00:13:00.461 --> 00:13:02.861
and adjust the strength
of the particle beam as we go.

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:04.727
That should minimize
the seismic stress

00:13:04.766 --> 00:13:06.666
that we'll generate
while we're drilling.

00:13:06.701 --> 00:13:08.430
Data, I reconfigured the phasers

00:13:08.469 --> 00:13:10.300
to create
the most highly focused

00:13:10.338 --> 00:13:11.600
particle beam possible.

00:13:11.639 --> 00:13:13.197
Thank you, Geordi.

00:13:14.242 --> 00:13:16.608
I'm just so pleased
you've got good manners.

00:13:16.644 --> 00:13:18.874
It wasn't easy to strike
the right balance

00:13:18.946 --> 00:13:20.436
with your programming.

00:13:20.481 --> 00:13:23.177
Well, at first, you
couldn't have cared less

00:13:23.217 --> 00:13:26.880
about the social niceties
like "please" and "thank you."

00:13:26.921 --> 00:13:29.014
You were downright rude,
in fact.

00:13:29.057 --> 00:13:30.217
Data?

00:13:30.258 --> 00:13:32.692
Well, that's hard to picture.

00:13:32.727 --> 00:13:34.160
Well, that was nothing

00:13:34.195 --> 00:13:36.959
to the problems
we encountered...

00:13:37.999 --> 00:13:39.125
Never mind.

00:13:39.167 --> 00:13:41.192
I don't want to embarrass you.

00:13:41.235 --> 00:13:43.465
I am incapable
of embarrassment.

00:13:43.504 --> 00:13:46.302
Please continue.

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:50.367
Well, the one thing
that we couldn't anticipate

00:13:50.411 --> 00:13:52.811
was that you didn't seem
to mind about being

00:13:52.847 --> 00:13:53.973
uh... naked.

00:13:55.249 --> 00:13:57.217
Some of the colonists
objected to having

00:13:57.251 --> 00:14:00.084
an anatomically correct
android running around

00:14:00.121 --> 00:14:01.713
without any clothes on.

00:14:01.756 --> 00:14:04.816
Oh, we asked you to dress

00:14:04.859 --> 00:14:06.554
but you didn't feel
it was necessary

00:14:06.594 --> 00:14:09.529
because you didn't suffer
from the elements.

00:14:09.564 --> 00:14:12.863
We actually had to write
a modesty subroutine

00:14:12.900 --> 00:14:15.494
to get you to keep
your clothes on.

00:14:15.536 --> 00:14:17.595
Riker to Engineering.

00:14:17.638 --> 00:14:19.868
La Forge here.
Go ahead, Commander.

00:14:19.907 --> 00:14:23.741
We've established synchronous
orbit over the drilling site.

00:14:23.778 --> 00:14:26.212
Phaser modifications
are on line, sir.

00:14:26.247 --> 00:14:29.705
My calculations indicate
that the first phaser blast

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:32.480
will be approximately
19 seconds in duration.

00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:33.748
Acknowledged.

00:14:33.788 --> 00:14:36.689
Someone's checked
his calculations, of course.

00:14:36.724 --> 00:14:39.818
No, but I'm sure Mr. Data
knows what he's doing.

00:14:39.861 --> 00:14:41.829
Even so, he is a machine.

00:14:41.863 --> 00:14:44.388
Someone should check up on him.

00:14:44.432 --> 00:14:47.401
I have complete confidence
in Mr. Data's ability

00:14:47.435 --> 00:14:48.868
to check up on himself.

00:14:48.903 --> 00:14:50.029
Mr. Worf?

00:14:50.071 --> 00:14:52.062
Phasers locked on target.

00:14:52.106 --> 00:14:53.971
Fire when ready.

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:03.073
We are within two kilometers
of the magma pocket.

00:15:03.117 --> 00:15:06.143
Another five seconds
should do it.

00:15:07.855 --> 00:15:09.254
We've broken through.

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:11.121
Terminating the beam.

00:15:11.159 --> 00:15:14.856
Oh, the pocket seems stable.

00:15:14.962 --> 00:15:16.020
I detect no increase

00:15:16.063 --> 00:15:18.531
in the stress levels
of the surrounding magma.

00:15:18.566 --> 00:15:19.863
Good work, Data.

00:15:19.901 --> 00:15:22.096
I don't think we could
have gotten in any cleaner.

00:15:22.136 --> 00:15:23.501
We have Data to thank for that.

00:15:23.538 --> 00:15:24.869
I couldn't have done it
without him.

00:15:24.939 --> 00:15:26.668
His figures were perfect.

00:15:27.675 --> 00:15:28.767
The drilling process

00:15:28.809 --> 00:15:30.868
has increased the temperature
in the magma pockets

00:15:30.978 --> 00:15:32.809
by almost 300 degrees Celsius.

00:15:32.847 --> 00:15:34.144
It will be several hours

00:15:34.182 --> 00:15:36.309
before it cools enough
for us to enter.

00:15:41.822 --> 00:15:44.256
Data, do you have
any plans right now?

00:15:44.292 --> 00:15:45.520
I do not.

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:48.893
Maybe we should spend
a little time together.

00:15:48.996 --> 00:15:51.794
I'd love to see your quarters.

00:16:31.272 --> 00:16:33.763
Thank you.
I will be playing this piece

00:16:33.808 --> 00:16:35.776
at a recital tomorrow evening.

00:16:35.810 --> 00:16:37.744
That was beautiful.

00:16:37.778 --> 00:16:41.646
Hmm. I have been told that my
playing is technically flawless

00:16:41.682 --> 00:16:44.617
but no one has ever described it
as beautiful.

00:16:44.652 --> 00:16:47.120
It was. Really.

00:16:47.154 --> 00:16:49.554
Are you certain
you are not saying this

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:51.251
because you are my mother?

00:16:53.894 --> 00:16:56.385
I have noticed
that parents tend to exaggerate

00:16:56.430 --> 00:16:59.160
when it comes to their
children's accomplishments.

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:04.194
Oh, I suppose there's a certain
amount of vanity involved

00:17:04.238 --> 00:17:09.403
considering that giving you
a creative aspect was my idea.

00:17:09.443 --> 00:17:12.435
Oh, your father didn't really
see the point.

00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:15.677
He thought that since
you didn't have emotions

00:17:15.716 --> 00:17:19.584
there would be no real need
for you to express yourself.

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:23.579
Somehow, I had the feeling
that the opposite would be true.

00:17:25.359 --> 00:17:27.327
I do not know for certain

00:17:27.361 --> 00:17:31.127
but I believe it is during
my creative endeavors

00:17:31.165 --> 00:17:33.861
that I come closest
to experiencing

00:17:33.901 --> 00:17:36.461
what it must be like
to be human.

00:17:36.504 --> 00:17:40.964
Well, I'm glad I insisted.

00:17:41.008 --> 00:17:43.476
As am I.

00:17:46.414 --> 00:17:48.245
Data...

00:17:48.282 --> 00:17:51.046
I'm very familiar
with that Handel piece.

00:17:51.085 --> 00:17:52.746
How would you feel about

00:17:52.787 --> 00:17:55.153
my playing the viola part
tomorrow?

00:17:55.189 --> 00:17:57.350
I would like that very much.

00:17:57.391 --> 00:17:59.325
Well, I'll have to practice.

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:01.555
You don't happen to have
a viola?

00:18:01.595 --> 00:18:03.859
I could replicate one for you.

00:18:07.001 --> 00:18:09.799
Computer, please
replicate one viola.

00:18:13.441 --> 00:18:15.375
Did you paint these?

00:18:15.409 --> 00:18:16.774
Yes.

00:18:16.811 --> 00:18:20.338
I am attempting to master
all known styles of painting.

00:18:20.381 --> 00:18:22.076
Oh!

00:18:22.116 --> 00:18:23.640
This one is in the style

00:18:23.684 --> 00:18:25.982
of the early French
Impressionists.

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:27.647
Oh, it's very good.

00:18:28.923 --> 00:18:30.788
Who's this?

00:18:30.825 --> 00:18:34.261
That is Lal, my daughter.

00:18:34.295 --> 00:18:37.059
Your daughter?

00:18:37.098 --> 00:18:40.067
I created her
using myself as a model.

00:18:41.535 --> 00:18:43.901
Where is she now?

00:18:45.306 --> 00:18:49.299
The positronic matrix
I designed for her was unstable.

00:18:49.343 --> 00:18:51.504
She only lived a short time.

00:18:53.381 --> 00:18:55.474
I see.

00:18:55.516 --> 00:18:59.282
In a sense,
you were her grandmother.

00:19:03.691 --> 00:19:06.159
Would you like to practice now?

00:19:07.261 --> 00:19:09.786
Yes. Yes, of course.

00:19:36.990 --> 00:19:40.084
The acoustics in Ten-Forward
are most favorable.

00:19:40.126 --> 00:19:42.754
Yes. Yes, very nice.

00:19:43.797 --> 00:19:46.357
Data, may I ask you something?

00:19:46.399 --> 00:19:48.333
Of course.

00:19:48.368 --> 00:19:49.995
Do you think
you'll ever try to create

00:19:50.036 --> 00:19:51.333
an android again?

00:19:52.605 --> 00:19:54.505
Perhaps.

00:19:54.541 --> 00:19:57.669
I created Lal
because I wished to procreate.

00:19:57.711 --> 00:20:01.579
Despite what happened to her,
I still have that wish.

00:20:01.614 --> 00:20:05.380
But how do you know
the same thing won't happen?

00:20:05.418 --> 00:20:09.684
Creating a stable positron
matrix is very tricky.

00:20:09.723 --> 00:20:13.215
Your father lost
several prototypes before Lore.

00:20:13.259 --> 00:20:17.855
I was not aware he created other
androids before my brother.

00:20:20.934 --> 00:20:23.425
There were three of them.

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:26.769
They were like children to us.

00:20:26.806 --> 00:20:30.071
Losing them was very painful.

00:20:30.110 --> 00:20:32.340
When Noonien decided
to try again

00:20:32.379 --> 00:20:34.313
I was very much against it.

00:20:34.347 --> 00:20:38.681
I didn't think we had the right
to bring a life into the world

00:20:38.718 --> 00:20:41.152
with so little chance
of surviving.

00:20:41.187 --> 00:20:43.348
But your father was sure

00:20:43.390 --> 00:20:46.791
that he'd figured out
what went wrong.

00:20:46.826 --> 00:20:53.095
He insisted he could make
a stable matrix, and he did.

00:20:53.133 --> 00:20:57.729
But Lore was... cruel...

00:20:57.771 --> 00:21:00.069
evil.

00:21:00.106 --> 00:21:02.700
Eventually, we had no choice.

00:21:02.742 --> 00:21:05.040
We had to dismantle him.

00:21:05.078 --> 00:21:08.536
Your father decided to build
yet another android...

00:21:08.581 --> 00:21:10.708
one who didn't have emotions.

00:21:10.750 --> 00:21:14.481
I couldn't believe...
he would want to try again.

00:21:14.521 --> 00:21:17.319
I am that android.

00:21:19.392 --> 00:21:22.327
Are you saying you were
against my creation?

00:21:24.297 --> 00:21:26.731
Initially I was,
but I was wrong.

00:21:26.766 --> 00:21:28.734
I know that now.

00:21:31.004 --> 00:21:35.498
I followed
your progress for years.

00:21:35.542 --> 00:21:38.568
I'm very proud
of what you've accomplished.

00:21:38.611 --> 00:21:41.876
Then, why did you never
attempt to contact me?

00:21:44.050 --> 00:21:47.645
Because I felt guilty
about something I'd done.

00:21:49.022 --> 00:21:52.150
Perhaps if you told me
what has made you feel this way

00:21:52.192 --> 00:21:54.057
it would alleviate the guilt.

00:21:56.529 --> 00:21:58.429
I lied...

00:21:58.465 --> 00:22:00.865
when I said there
was no room for you

00:22:00.900 --> 00:22:04.131
in the escape pod
we took from Omicron.

00:22:04.170 --> 00:22:07.571
There was.

00:22:09.542 --> 00:22:12.340
I didn't want
to bring you with us.

00:22:15.748 --> 00:22:19.081
I was afraid
if we reactivated you

00:22:19.119 --> 00:22:21.713
you'd turn out like Lore.

00:22:26.126 --> 00:22:29.095
I made Noonien leave you behind.

00:22:49.949 --> 00:22:53.385
We are within four kilometers
of the magma pocket.

00:22:53.419 --> 00:22:57.048
We're picking up feedback pulses
along the particle beam.

00:22:57.089 --> 00:22:59.023
We must have hit a pocket
of magnesite ore.

00:22:59.058 --> 00:23:01.583
I'll try to adjust the phaser
harmonics to compensate.

00:23:01.627 --> 00:23:03.026
Data, we're going to have

00:23:03.062 --> 00:23:04.757
to terminate the beam
if this keeps up.

00:23:04.797 --> 00:23:06.731
If we do, we will have
to begin a new shaft

00:23:06.766 --> 00:23:07.790
at a suitable location.

00:23:07.834 --> 00:23:09.859
There is
no other suitable location.

00:23:09.902 --> 00:23:11.836
Just give me a few more seconds.

00:23:13.873 --> 00:23:18.367
Doctor, it's going to take
longer than that to match the...

00:23:18.411 --> 00:23:20.174
You did it.

00:23:20.213 --> 00:23:23.011
It was just luck
I hit the right frequency.

00:23:23.049 --> 00:23:25.540
All right, we're less
than two kilometers away

00:23:25.585 --> 00:23:27.075
from the target site.

00:23:27.119 --> 00:23:29.212
Stand by to terminate the beam.

00:23:30.389 --> 00:23:31.879
We've broken through.

00:23:31.958 --> 00:23:33.516
Now!

00:23:34.760 --> 00:23:37.558
I am detecting no signs
of instability.

00:23:37.597 --> 00:23:40.395
Commander, may I suggest
we set up the infusion unit

00:23:40.433 --> 00:23:41.798
in the first magma pocket

00:23:41.834 --> 00:23:44.064
and give this one
a chance to cool?

00:23:44.103 --> 00:23:45.331
Data, Dr. Tainer

00:23:45.371 --> 00:23:47.896
we'll meet you
in Transporter Room Two.

00:23:48.007 --> 00:23:49.497
Acknowledged.

00:24:01.787 --> 00:24:04.756
I have initialized
the plasma induction coils.

00:24:04.790 --> 00:24:07.850
I'll need another minute
to align the diverter.

00:24:17.069 --> 00:24:20.300
There are signs of stress
in the surrounding magma

00:24:20.339 --> 00:24:22.432
but the site
should remain stable

00:24:22.475 --> 00:24:24.773
until we finish
the plasma infusion.

00:24:24.810 --> 00:24:26.300
Good.
We're almost through here.

00:24:26.345 --> 00:24:28.108
Data...

00:24:29.815 --> 00:24:33.114
Juliana told me what she
said to you last night.

00:24:33.152 --> 00:24:35.450
She's been very upset.

00:24:35.488 --> 00:24:37.820
I don't blame you
for being angry with her...

00:24:37.857 --> 00:24:39.449
I am incapable of anger.

00:24:39.492 --> 00:24:41.687
It's all right, Pran.

00:24:45.197 --> 00:24:46.494
I know what I said to you

00:24:46.532 --> 00:24:48.329
must have been hard
for you to hear

00:24:48.367 --> 00:24:52.030
but I hope you understand
my reasons.

00:24:53.205 --> 00:24:55.799
I am not certain I do.

00:24:55.841 --> 00:24:58.275
Perhaps you could
clarify them for me.

00:24:58.311 --> 00:25:00.973
Well, I'll try.
What do you want to know?

00:25:01.013 --> 00:25:03.948
If I had been
your biological offspring

00:25:03.983 --> 00:25:06.713
would you have left me
on Omicron Theta?

00:25:08.955 --> 00:25:10.980
Oh, Data...

00:25:11.023 --> 00:25:12.752
how can I answer that?

00:25:12.792 --> 00:25:15.488
Dr. Tainer, I get the impression

00:25:15.528 --> 00:25:18.190
you are trying
to spare my feelings.

00:25:18.230 --> 00:25:21.563
I assure you
that is not necessary.

00:25:21.601 --> 00:25:24.968
I just don't want you
to misunderstand my answer.

00:25:27.540 --> 00:25:29.872
No, I wouldn't have
left you behind

00:25:29.909 --> 00:25:32.241
if you'd been
my biological child.

00:25:32.278 --> 00:25:35.577
Hmm. Is that because you place
more value

00:25:35.615 --> 00:25:38.846
on biological life
than artificial life?

00:25:38.884 --> 00:25:41.216
Absolutely not.

00:25:41.253 --> 00:25:44.381
I cherished every android
your father and I created

00:25:44.423 --> 00:25:45.890
as if it were my child.

00:25:45.925 --> 00:25:47.051
Even Lore.

00:25:47.093 --> 00:25:49.391
Despite the fact
that he turned on us

00:25:49.428 --> 00:25:51.225
despite the dreadful
things he did

00:25:51.263 --> 00:25:52.560
dismantling him was

00:25:52.598 --> 00:25:54.293
was the most difficult thing
I ever had to do.

00:25:54.333 --> 00:25:55.891
I was afraid that if you
turned out like him

00:25:56.002 --> 00:25:58.163
I would have
to dismantle you, too.

00:26:02.375 --> 00:26:05.173
And I couldn't bear to do that.

00:26:08.280 --> 00:26:12.478
I'm not trying to justify
leaving you behind.

00:26:12.518 --> 00:26:16.010
I'm just sorry I did.

00:26:16.055 --> 00:26:17.852
I hope you believe me.

00:26:17.957 --> 00:26:20.391
I do.

00:26:20.426 --> 00:26:22.894
Thank you for making
it clear to me.

00:27:17.383 --> 00:27:18.475
Just wonderful.

00:27:18.517 --> 00:27:19.506
Bravo.

00:27:26.792 --> 00:27:29.727
Data, why do you want to look
at Dr. Tainer's medical records?

00:27:29.762 --> 00:27:31.024
Is something wrong with her?

00:27:31.063 --> 00:27:33.327
I was hoping you would be able
to determine that

00:27:33.365 --> 00:27:34.957
from her transporter
trace pattern.

00:27:35.000 --> 00:27:36.058
Well, probably I could

00:27:36.102 --> 00:27:37.467
but ordinarily I don't check

00:27:37.503 --> 00:27:39.869
somebody's medical status
without a good reason.

00:27:39.905 --> 00:27:42.567
Doctor, I would ask
that you not require me

00:27:42.608 --> 00:27:44.098
to be more specific.

00:27:44.143 --> 00:27:45.770
I assure you

00:27:45.811 --> 00:27:48.507
I have a good reason for asking.

00:27:48.547 --> 00:27:50.242
All right, Data.

00:27:59.892 --> 00:28:02.725
At first glance,
I see nothing wrong with her

00:28:02.762 --> 00:28:05.253
except for a mild case
of hypertension

00:28:05.297 --> 00:28:07.629
which is normal
for a woman her age.

00:28:07.666 --> 00:28:08.826
I see.

00:28:08.934 --> 00:28:11.960
Maybe you should tell me
what her symptoms are.

00:28:12.004 --> 00:28:15.030
She has not complained
of any discomfort.

00:28:15.074 --> 00:28:18.271
Then why do you want to
see her medical records?

00:28:18.310 --> 00:28:22.337
Because I have reason to believe
she is not who she claims to be.

00:28:22.381 --> 00:28:23.848
Bridge to Data.

00:28:23.916 --> 00:28:25.406
Go ahead, sir.

00:28:25.451 --> 00:28:27.646
There's been a cave-in
in one of the magma pockets.

00:28:27.686 --> 00:28:29.347
You're needed
in Transporter Room Two.

00:28:29.388 --> 00:28:30.355
On my way.

00:28:30.389 --> 00:28:31.617
Excuse me, Doctor.

00:28:38.897 --> 00:28:40.797
What happened?

00:28:40.832 --> 00:28:43.494
We were running a final check
on the infusion units

00:28:43.535 --> 00:28:45.298
when a part
of the wall gave way.

00:28:45.336 --> 00:28:46.860
It looks like the area
has stabilized

00:28:46.905 --> 00:28:48.304
but seismic stress is
building up.

00:28:48.339 --> 00:28:49.863
Eventually the pocket
will collapse.

00:28:49.908 --> 00:28:52.206
How long, Geordi?

00:28:52.243 --> 00:28:54.268
It's tough to tell, Commander.

00:28:54.312 --> 00:28:56.212
12 hours at most.

00:28:56.247 --> 00:28:58.408
Then we must finish
configuring the unit

00:28:58.450 --> 00:29:00.577
and inject the plasma
immediately.

00:29:00.618 --> 00:29:03.485
I'd rather not send
anyone back down there.

00:29:03.521 --> 00:29:05.250
If you don't do it
now, Commander

00:29:05.290 --> 00:29:07.918
it may take months to find
another suitable site.

00:29:07.959 --> 00:29:09.517
The core may solidify by then.

00:29:09.561 --> 00:29:11.324
She's right.
We have to act now.

00:29:11.362 --> 00:29:13.421
All right, but I want you
in and out of there

00:29:13.465 --> 00:29:14.557
as quickly as possible.

00:29:14.599 --> 00:29:15.759
Acknowledged.

00:29:15.800 --> 00:29:17.392
You're hurt.
I'll go.

00:30:02.981 --> 00:30:05.279
There will be
more seismic activity.

00:30:05.316 --> 00:30:06.749
We must hurry.

00:30:35.947 --> 00:30:40.281
The shaft has not been
obstructed by seismic activity.

00:30:40.318 --> 00:30:42.752
It should be possible
to trigger the unit from orbit.

00:30:42.787 --> 00:30:44.414
The infuser's been damaged.

00:30:44.455 --> 00:30:46.184
We're going to have to start

00:30:46.224 --> 00:30:48.283
the programming sequence
all over again.

00:30:49.627 --> 00:30:51.185
Priming the energy
transfer matrix.

00:30:51.229 --> 00:30:54.858
Reinitializing
the particle stream buffer.

00:30:54.899 --> 00:30:56.196
Riker to Data.
Are you there?

00:30:56.234 --> 00:30:58.031
Go ahead, sir.

00:30:58.069 --> 00:31:01.664
We're reading an increase
in seismic stress levels.

00:31:01.706 --> 00:31:02.798
Understood, sir.

00:31:02.840 --> 00:31:04.740
We will attempt to expedite
our work.

00:31:05.977 --> 00:31:10.175
There. Now we just have
to realign the diverter.

00:31:14.052 --> 00:31:15.815
Data, are you all right?

00:31:18.423 --> 00:31:20.050
Yes, sir.

00:31:20.091 --> 00:31:24.221
We will be returning
to the beam-out point shortly.

00:31:24.262 --> 00:31:25.752
That's it. Let's go.

00:31:42.981 --> 00:31:44.881
Can we transport
without the pattern enhancers?

00:31:44.916 --> 00:31:48.784
No. We are too far
below the surface.

00:31:48.820 --> 00:31:51.687
How are we going
to get down there?

00:31:51.723 --> 00:31:54.988
There are no handholds
in the rock face.

00:31:57.195 --> 00:31:58.924
We are going to have to jump.

00:31:58.997 --> 00:32:01.090
No. It's too far,
I won't make it.

00:32:01.132 --> 00:32:02.224
You will.

00:32:26.056 --> 00:32:28.991
Basically,
she's a Soong-type android

00:32:29.026 --> 00:32:30.459
except everything about her

00:32:30.494 --> 00:32:33.156
is designed to fool you
into thinking she's human.

00:32:36.834 --> 00:32:40.065
She has tear ducts,
sweat glands

00:32:40.104 --> 00:32:44.541
even veins and capillaries
underneath her skin.

00:32:44.575 --> 00:32:46.475
Why does the scanner
read her as human?

00:32:46.510 --> 00:32:48.808
Because she has
a feedback processor

00:32:48.846 --> 00:32:51.212
designed to send out
a false bio-signal.

00:32:51.248 --> 00:32:53.443
It's part of her aging program.

00:32:53.484 --> 00:32:56.248
Not only does she age
in appearance like Data

00:32:56.287 --> 00:32:58.881
her vital signs change, too.

00:32:58.922 --> 00:33:03.359
What I can't figure out
is why she lost consciousness.

00:33:03.394 --> 00:33:05.624
As far as I can see,
everything is fine.

00:33:05.663 --> 00:33:06.960
She should be awake.

00:33:06.997 --> 00:33:09.090
Check her positronic matrix.

00:33:09.133 --> 00:33:11.795
There may be a cascade anomaly.

00:33:11.835 --> 00:33:15.396
You said you knew
she was an android. How?

00:33:15.439 --> 00:33:18.670
The first indication occurred
when we were digging.

00:33:18.709 --> 00:33:21.177
I saw her perform
complex calculations

00:33:21.211 --> 00:33:23.702
without the assistance
of the computer.

00:33:23.747 --> 00:33:26.147
That could have just meant
she was good at math.

00:33:26.183 --> 00:33:27.150
That is true.

00:33:27.184 --> 00:33:29.015
But it was enough
to get my attention.

00:33:29.053 --> 00:33:30.520
Later, I noticed something odd

00:33:30.554 --> 00:33:32.818
about the way
she blinked her eyes.

00:33:32.856 --> 00:33:34.517
The intervals between blinks

00:33:34.558 --> 00:33:36.822
were governed
by the Fourier system...

00:33:36.860 --> 00:33:39.260
the same mathematical formula
my father used

00:33:39.296 --> 00:33:42.493
to give my blinking pattern
the appearance of randomness.

00:33:42.533 --> 00:33:45.263
Only you could have noticed
something like that.

00:33:45.302 --> 00:33:47.998
Then there was
the concert in Ten-Forward.

00:33:48.038 --> 00:33:49.335
What about it?

00:33:49.373 --> 00:33:52.069
We had practiced the piece,
and I noticed

00:33:52.109 --> 00:33:54.805
she played it the same way
during the performance...

00:33:54.845 --> 00:33:57.575
every pitch, every intonation
was exactly the same.

00:33:57.614 --> 00:34:00.310
Only an artificial life-form
could have done that.

00:34:01.251 --> 00:34:03.776
Does her husband
know anything about this?

00:34:03.821 --> 00:34:06.312
I do not believe so.

00:34:06.357 --> 00:34:09.588
He is on the surface monitoring
the plasma infusion.

00:34:09.626 --> 00:34:11.389
Probably just as well.

00:34:11.428 --> 00:34:14.363
Data, come take a look at this.

00:34:18.569 --> 00:34:21.129
It appears to be
an information module.

00:34:23.774 --> 00:34:26.937
With a holographic interface.

00:34:46.029 --> 00:34:47.462
Whoever you are

00:34:47.498 --> 00:34:50.365
you must have found out
about Juliana.

00:34:50.401 --> 00:34:51.698
That is correct.

00:34:51.735 --> 00:34:53.999
I programmed this hologram

00:34:54.037 --> 00:34:57.370
to answer any questions
you might have.

00:34:57.408 --> 00:35:00.002
I am Noonien Soong.

00:35:00.043 --> 00:35:01.374
I created her.

00:35:01.412 --> 00:35:03.505
I am Data.

00:35:03.547 --> 00:35:07.381
Data?

00:35:07.418 --> 00:35:10.683
I hoped somehow it would be you.

00:35:15.993 --> 00:35:19.622
I even created
a response program

00:35:19.663 --> 00:35:22.530
to answer your questions.

00:35:28.806 --> 00:35:30.239
How are you, boy?

00:35:30.274 --> 00:35:32.401
I am fine.

00:35:32.443 --> 00:35:36.539
I'm glad you got the chance
to meet your mother.

00:35:36.580 --> 00:35:39.276
You refer to Dr. Tainer
as my mother

00:35:39.316 --> 00:35:42.410
yet the complexity
of her design indicates

00:35:42.453 --> 00:35:44.614
she was created after I was.

00:35:45.622 --> 00:35:47.317
You're right.

00:35:47.357 --> 00:35:50.019
But...

00:35:50.060 --> 00:35:53.427
there was
a real Juliana O'Donnell.

00:35:56.633 --> 00:36:00.091
She was my wife.

00:36:00.137 --> 00:36:01.832
She helped me create you.

00:36:01.939 --> 00:36:04.601
What happened to her?

00:36:08.479 --> 00:36:12.848
She was... injured

00:36:12.950 --> 00:36:15.714
when the Crystalline Entity
attacked.

00:36:15.752 --> 00:36:18.516
We made it as far as Terlina III

00:36:18.555 --> 00:36:19.920
but...

00:36:22.125 --> 00:36:24.616
she slipped into a coma.

00:36:25.729 --> 00:36:27.128
When I realized

00:36:27.164 --> 00:36:31.362
nothing could be done for her,
I built an android.

00:36:33.136 --> 00:36:37.971
I tried to... perfect
my synaptic scanning technique

00:36:38.008 --> 00:36:42.001
so that I could transfer
Juliana's memories

00:36:42.045 --> 00:36:43.603
into a positronic matrix.

00:36:43.647 --> 00:36:45.478
Didn't know if it would work

00:36:45.516 --> 00:36:47.484
but I had to try.

00:36:49.953 --> 00:36:52.080
I couldn't stand the thought

00:36:52.122 --> 00:36:54.955
of losing the only woman
I ever loved.

00:36:57.561 --> 00:37:01.156
A few days after Juliana died,
I activated the android.

00:37:04.535 --> 00:37:07.766
She looked up at me...

00:37:07.804 --> 00:37:10.739
and smiled.

00:37:10.774 --> 00:37:13.140
She recognized me.

00:37:13.176 --> 00:37:15.303
It had worked!

00:37:15.345 --> 00:37:17.836
Here was a life
not two minutes old

00:37:17.881 --> 00:37:21.544
and as far as she was concerned,
I was her husband.

00:37:21.585 --> 00:37:24.782
She'd just recovered
from a terrible injury.

00:37:24.821 --> 00:37:27.722
It was incredible.

00:37:27.758 --> 00:37:29.851
Then you never told her
the truth?

00:37:29.960 --> 00:37:32.190
Why?

00:37:32.229 --> 00:37:35.721
There was no reason
for her to know.

00:37:35.766 --> 00:37:37.961
I wanted her to be happy.

00:37:39.970 --> 00:37:43.633
I wanted us to be happy.

00:37:43.674 --> 00:37:45.164
And we were...

00:37:49.879 --> 00:37:51.141
...for awhile.

00:37:51.180 --> 00:37:52.579
What happened?

00:37:57.686 --> 00:38:00.018
I made a terrible mistake.

00:38:02.625 --> 00:38:05.822
I never really...

00:38:05.895 --> 00:38:08.887
let her know
how much I loved her.

00:38:11.100 --> 00:38:12.897
So she left me.

00:38:14.904 --> 00:38:17.270
The real Juliana
would have left, too

00:38:17.306 --> 00:38:18.830
if she had lived.

00:38:18.941 --> 00:38:22.240
If she recovers and learns
that she is an android...

00:38:22.278 --> 00:38:25.145
She doesn't have to know.

00:38:25.181 --> 00:38:27.775
Now, I designed her to shut down

00:38:27.817 --> 00:38:30.980
in the event that the truth
was discovered.

00:38:31.020 --> 00:38:34.046
When you... when you
put that chip back in

00:38:34.090 --> 00:38:37.253
she will wake up
and remember nothing.

00:38:37.293 --> 00:38:40.194
All you have to do
is make up some excuse

00:38:40.229 --> 00:38:42.197
about what happened to her.

00:38:42.231 --> 00:38:45.632
Then you do not believe
she should know the truth?

00:38:45.668 --> 00:38:47.295
The truth.

00:38:49.505 --> 00:38:51.370
The truth is

00:38:51.407 --> 00:38:54.865
in every way that matters

00:38:54.910 --> 00:38:57.970
she is Juliana Soong.

00:39:00.850 --> 00:39:05.150
I programmed her to terminate
after a long life.

00:39:05.187 --> 00:39:08.645
Let her live out her days

00:39:08.691 --> 00:39:13.424
and die believing she was human.

00:39:13.462 --> 00:39:17.489
Don't rob her of that, son...

00:39:17.533 --> 00:39:20.001
please.

00:39:20.102 --> 00:39:22.627
It seems that I must
make a decision...

00:39:22.671 --> 00:39:26.038
whether to tell Dr. Tainer
that she is an android

00:39:26.075 --> 00:39:28.942
or to withhold
that information from her.

00:39:31.113 --> 00:39:32.978
I do not know what to do.

00:39:33.015 --> 00:39:36.109
Why was Dr. Soong so adamant
that she not be told?

00:39:36.152 --> 00:39:38.313
He seemed certain
that if she knew

00:39:38.354 --> 00:39:40.549
it would preclude the
possibility of her being happy.

00:39:40.589 --> 00:39:42.181
Data, what do you think?

00:39:42.224 --> 00:39:43.851
I am not certain.

00:39:43.893 --> 00:39:46.589
I understand why my father
felt as he did

00:39:46.629 --> 00:39:49.564
but his wishes are not
necessarily paramount.

00:39:49.598 --> 00:39:52.761
I am more concerned
with what would be best for her.

00:39:52.801 --> 00:39:56.532
Wouldn't she be better off
knowing the truth

00:39:56.572 --> 00:39:59.132
dealing with the reality
of her existence?

00:39:59.175 --> 00:40:00.437
I don't think so.

00:40:00.476 --> 00:40:03.036
She's believed
she's human all her life.

00:40:03.078 --> 00:40:05.512
The truth might be
devastating to her.

00:40:05.548 --> 00:40:08.711
Data, there might come
some time in the future

00:40:08.751 --> 00:40:12.812
when she would find out anyway...
another accident, perhaps.

00:40:12.855 --> 00:40:15.119
Maybe it would be easier for her

00:40:15.157 --> 00:40:18.126
if she learned
the truth from you.

00:40:18.160 --> 00:40:21.687
I can tell you
that if I were in her place

00:40:21.730 --> 00:40:26.394
I would rather be told by my son
than by some stranger.

00:40:29.772 --> 00:40:32.605
I find I am having
difficulty separating

00:40:32.641 --> 00:40:36.600
what would be best for her

00:40:36.645 --> 00:40:38.738
from what would be best for me.

00:40:38.781 --> 00:40:40.112
What do you mean?

00:40:40.149 --> 00:40:43.209
If she knew she were an android

00:40:43.252 --> 00:40:46.415
we would have
something to share.

00:40:46.455 --> 00:40:49.356
I would no longer
be alone in the universe.

00:40:53.963 --> 00:40:57.899
I know how much
that means to you, Data

00:40:57.933 --> 00:41:00.766
but at the same time,
by telling her

00:41:00.803 --> 00:41:03.533
you're robbing her
of the one thing

00:41:03.572 --> 00:41:05.870
you've wanted all your life...

00:41:05.975 --> 00:41:08.273
to be human.

00:41:11.313 --> 00:41:13.440
It's a difficult choice.

00:41:13.482 --> 00:41:15.882
You must do
what you think best, Data.

00:41:15.985 --> 00:41:19.386
But whatever decision you make,
we will support it.

00:41:45.881 --> 00:41:48.782
Data.

00:41:48.817 --> 00:41:51.183
What happened?

00:41:51.220 --> 00:41:55.350
The last thing I remember
was jumping off a cliff.

00:41:56.825 --> 00:41:58.690
You were knocked unconscious
by the fall.

00:42:00.629 --> 00:42:03.291
You broke a bone in your arm

00:42:03.332 --> 00:42:05.323
but Dr. Crusher repaired it.

00:42:10.072 --> 00:42:11.664
Everything is fine.

00:42:15.711 --> 00:42:18.407
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:42:18.447 --> 00:42:21.473
The infusion of plasma
into the core of Atrea IV

00:42:21.517 --> 00:42:22.882
has been accomplished.

00:42:22.918 --> 00:42:26.183
The core should remain molten
for several hundred years.

00:42:26.221 --> 00:42:28.712
When will I see you again?

00:42:28.757 --> 00:42:32.454
Perhaps I can visit Atrea
on my next leave.

00:42:32.494 --> 00:42:35.190
I would like that very much.

00:42:37.933 --> 00:42:39.924
Well, I'd better be going.

00:42:41.503 --> 00:42:44.563
There is something
I think you should know.

00:42:44.606 --> 00:42:46.904
My father told me...

00:42:49.878 --> 00:42:52.870
that he had only one
great love in his life

00:42:52.915 --> 00:42:55.543
and that he regretted
never telling her

00:42:55.584 --> 00:42:57.415
how much he cared for her.

00:42:59.154 --> 00:43:03.147
I am certain he was
referring to you.

00:43:08.263 --> 00:43:10.458
That's nice to know.

00:43:13.535 --> 00:43:15.799
On Atrea, there is a saying

00:43:15.838 --> 00:43:20.832
that a child born
from parents who love each other

00:43:20.876 --> 00:43:24.209
will have nothing
but goodness in his heart.

00:43:25.948 --> 00:43:28.473
I guess that explains you.

00:43:50.706 --> 00:43:52.606
Take care of yourself, son.

00:43:52.641 --> 00:43:55.940
Good-bye... Mother.

00:43:57.446 --> 00:43:59.277
Energize.
